*****************************************************************************/
The form incantations in IncantForms need to be reworked to work under kant; and the attributes referenced in those forms may need figuring out and may need a method/action written for them to work as intended.
Here is a list form attributes along with an explanation of what each attribute does. The list is derived from attributes in old GUI forms. Some of the attributes are part of the little drawing language (see drawing incantation). Attributes defined in templates tend to be mergeContainers that contain attributes that get merged into the mergeContainers parent on definition

    across              form field members will be laid out horizontally
    action              in old GUI seems to provide an onClick functionality but action will probably not make the transition from old GUI to kant where every attribute can have a method/action and we need to figure out how and when those get fired
    align               aligns text in the frame; allowed values: left center right;
    border              prints a rectangular border around the field; if border value is number that is used for its width;
                        an off value says no border but that is only relevant if border is inherited and probably it should not be inheritable
    button              a form component that acts as a button; has to have a method/action to fire when it gets clicked on (that implies a form component action works like an onClick action)
    cards               specifies that its parent contains cards that on display are layered on over the next with only one showing. The cards can be shuffled thru using arrow keys
    closable            makes a window or panel closable; should only work on windows or panels
    describe            used to link a field to its description in the dESCRIPTIONs registry. See descriptions incantation for how it works.
    doNotScroll         scroll block search goes bottom up looking for a scrollable block; doNotScroll means keep searching up
    down                form field members will be laid out vertically
    drawPath            says the attributes that follow it are drawing commands. Needs design and fleshing out.
    expander            references expandable and expanded attributes defined in templates. old GUI recon needed to figure out how expander works
    fit                 Wraps a container around its contents. A recon into old GUI (probably in Details.twk) needed to figure out how it works, and if we decide to keep it, how do we transfer its functionality to kant. Not a simple little attribute.
    flex                not sure what this does. Recon into old GUI needed to figure it out
    font                value is a font defined in the Fonts registry. updates current style
    key                 not sure what it does but it is used in layout (a forms incantation that needs figuring out)
    keyAction           says its container field has an action fired when the field is selected and a key is entered
    keyStroke           used to specify a keyStroke set; see keyStroke incantation. Some figuring out required.
    image               specifies the url or fie path of an image to be loaded
    matrix              requires an old GUI recon to figure out what it does. There are a number of matrix attributes defined in templates
    minimums            minimumHeight and minimumWidth constrain layout when checking if a component fits in its parent
    pad                 not planned to be supported in layout
    panel               like window but defines a panel to be displayed
    perforation         draws a perforated border on its parent using incant little drawing language
                            depth gap perfRight perfLeft perfTop perfBottom and stride are attributes used by perforation as parameters (they have default settings)
    popup               defines a popup box. How it works needs figuring. Recon into old GUI required.
    pullDown            fires a pull down menu. How it works needs figuring. Recon into old GUI required.
    radius              defines the radius used by rounded
    resize              makes a window or panel resizeable; should only work on windows or panels
    rounded             like border but puts up a rounded rectangle; the rounding radius should probably go into style
    selectable          flags its parent (a form component) as being selectable
    sort                takes a value that is the parent attribute to be sorted on??? Applies when multiple members involved to sort those members (the ones being displayed, not the source itself). sort will require a method/action to do the sorting. It will also require a recon thru old GUI to see how it used to work as first step to figuring out how it will work in kant.
    table attributes    defined in templates; include: tableBody tableCell tableHead tableLabel tableRow
    text                prints the form field text into its frame applying the current style
    title               as in title="Some Text" an attribute but title implies a different style; how to supply that implied style (presumably when title is defined, without the text data that get applied in a later redefinition when title is added to some field as an attribute). Does title have a method/action? If so what does it do?
    toggled             used in inspector form. recon into old GUI required to figure out what it does. May not transfer to kant.
    trait               interacts w/source. See layout incantation reference in the Forms Needing Figuring Out section below
    window              essentially the outermost field in a forms definition

/*****************************************************************************
    Form fields (not attributes) with special meaning
*****************************************************************************/
    form            is defined in templates; it probably should be renamed. Its design and use is interesting. The menu incantation makes use of it and warrants a look see to work thru.
    space           form field can have a numeric value; if its parent orientation is across, the value is its width; otherwise its height.
                    Typically, has no content. If has no value, its size if determined as its share of any residual space in its parent.
    comments        In old GUI form comments were flagged as ?text? We need a kant equivalent and can probably use normal quotes like // text

